                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2269a483-6df3-35c7-a6bb-d48edf7bfde1",
                        "entry_id": "c4bc8cee-5188-3ed7-8955-9d5bdb8d9a26",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Using casuistry or casuistics."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a561b4d9-f5fe-446b-af81-02793791593c",
                                "sense_id": "2269a483-6df3-35c7-a6bb-d48edf7bfde1",
                                "text": "He approached the moral dilemma casuistically, not abstractly from first principles."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4459088e-eae4-3eb0-914d-816e070b7f17",
                        "entry_id": "c4bc8cee-5188-3ed7-8955-9d5bdb8d9a26",
                        "glosses": [
                            "From the perspective of casuistics or casuistry."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3cee9763-2b0d-49c5-9eb9-b1896740963f",
                                "sense_id": "4459088e-eae4-3eb0-914d-816e070b7f17",
                                "text": "Those ideals are casuistically the best whose realisations lead to least number of other ideals sacrificed."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6a3d6949-3981-4dfe-bea5-b761f4fe5d76",
                                "sense_id": "4459088e-eae4-3eb0-914d-816e070b7f17",
                                "text": "Rule-utilitarian arguments — arguments that proceed from the consequences of our moral rules rather than of our individual acts — are casuistically very powerful."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c97dbcf4-8ebf-4460-812e-ecc1b39634ad",
                                "sense_id": "4459088e-eae4-3eb0-914d-816e070b7f17",
                                "text": "She would then be — casuistically, I suppose, and legally, without doubt — worse off than the seduced Isabella: for Isabella would have submitted to Angelo without consent of the will"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d6bb3453-d858-4e4b-8cbd-155129bf0e41",
                                "sense_id": "4459088e-eae4-3eb0-914d-816e070b7f17",
                                "text": "Critics may point out flaws in this story, which is casuistically vulnerable"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
